# grub -- the bootloader, and the only part of the ISO that firmware runs.
#
# EFI only, and that is a consequence rather than a preference: Duct's gcc is
# configured --disable-multilib, so there is no way to produce the 32-bit
# objects GRUB's i386-pc target is made of. A BIOS-bootable ISO would need
# either a multilib gcc or a second cross toolchain, and neither is worth it
# for firmware that has been superseded on every machine this distribution can
# currently be built on.
#
# What that costs is real and worth stating: the ISO does not boot on a
# pre-2012 PC, and it does not boot in a QEMU invocation that omits OVMF.
#
# Not an LFS-pinned source here -- grub is in the LFS book, but versions.env is
# generated from the LFS wget-list and grub is not in the package list Duct
# takes from it, so it is pinned in the recipe like every other addition.
SRC_URL=https://ftp.gnu.org/gnu/grub/grub-2.12.tar.xz
SRC_SHA256=f3c97391f7c4eaa677a78e090c7e97e6dc47b16f655f04683ebd37bef7fe0faa
SRC_DIR=grub-2.12
